      "description": "`parse_headers()` passes the advanced `p` from the truncated `Content` branch into `string_as_int32()`. With `s = data_copy + 32764`, this 4-byte memcpy reaches one byte past global `data_copy[32767]`, matching the saved ASan global-buffer-overflow READ of size 4."
